{"_id":"68a7362f8ec3d8323af1c567","nodeId":"soZFqivM3YBuljeX6PoaX","roadmapSlug":"python","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:26.571Z","description":"# Sets\n\nPython Set is an unordered collection of data types that is iterable, mutable, and has no duplicate elements. The order of elements in a set is undefined though it may consist of various elements. The major advantage of using a set, as opposed to a list, is that it has a highly optimized method for checking whether a specific element is contained in the set.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Python Official Documentation on Sets","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/datastructures.html#sets","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae391"},{"type":"article","title":"An In-Depth Guide to Working with Python Sets","url":"https://learnpython.com/blog/python-sets/","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae392"},{"type":"video","title":"Python Sets tutorial for Beginners","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t9j8lCUGZXo","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae393"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:09.455Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e33faacf8c05faf5e1fd0","title":"DataCamp - Python Programming Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/L0YnzL"},{"_id":"6a5e33fdacf8c05faf5e2124","title":"DataCamp - Python Developer","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/vDW623"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python/content/soZFqivM3YBuljeX6PoaX.md"}